# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.

# Your contact string, sent to SEC EDGAR as the User-Agent header.
#
# THIS IS NOT A SECRET. There is no SEC API key and no account to register.
# EDGAR asks automated clients to identify themselves with a way to get in
# touch, and that is all this is. It lives in .env only because it is personal
# to whoever is running the fetch, not because it needs protecting.
#
# It must be of the form "Name email@domain.com". EDGAR checks the shape: a
# missing or default User-Agent is answered with a 403 carrying an "Undeclared
# Automated Tool" page rather than the document you asked for. The fetcher
# refuses to start if this has no @ in it, so that failure arrives as a
# sentence rather than as unexplained 403s.
#
# The fetcher also sends "Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate", which the same SEC
# guidance asks for; that one is not configurable.
SEC_USER_AGENT=
